## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end CV system design under fintech constraints: latency, privacy, and robustness to occlusion and demographic variation.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular 3D face modeling and pose estimation
- On-device adaptation with few-shot learning
- Liveness detection under occlusion
- Synthetic+real data strategies, loss design, and evaluation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: brief outline of 3DMM fitting loop (high level)
function fit3DMM(frame, model) {
  const landmarks = detectLandmarks(frame);
  const pose = solvePnP(landmarks, model.meanShape);
  return {pose, coefficients: model.coeffs};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you design a privacy-preserving data pipeline for raw frames on-device?  
- Which metrics would you monitor in production to catch model drift or spoofing attempts?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical monocular depth reasoning and tracking in a simple inspection setting.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular depth proxy with known geometry
- Lightweight detectors, on-device adaptation
- Temporal tracking and data efficiency

## Code Example
```javascript
function projectTo3D(bbox, sheetDims, intrinsics) {
  // heuristic: depth proxy from vertical size and known sheet height
  const heightPx = bbox.height;
  const Z = (sheetDims.height * intrinsics.fy) / heightPx;
  return {X: 0, Y: 0, Z};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would occlusion or specular glare affect depth proxy? how to mitigate?
- How would you measure success and compare to a stereo baseline?

## Why This Question Is Asked

This question evaluates the ability to design a real-time monocular system integrating segmentation, 3D pose estimation with scene priors, grasp-point planning, and physics-based stability reasoning—plus efficient edge adaptation with minimal shots.

## Key Concepts

- Monocular 3D pose estimation using environmental priors
- Grasp-point prediction in cluttered scenes
- Differentiable physics modules for stability evaluation
- On-device few-shot adaptation strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode outline for the model heads
function forward(img, shelfPrior) {
  const features = backbone(img);
  const segmentation = segmentationHead(features);
  const pose = poseHead(features, shelfPrior);
  const grasp = graspHead(features, pose);
  const stability = physicsPrior(grasp, pose);
  return { segmentation, pose, grasp, stability };
}
```
